THE KRAIT OBJECT SERIALIZATION LANGUAGE (KOSL) TL;DR

  - KraitDev owns the official Krait Object Serialization Language (KOSL)
    project.

  - Anyone can use, modify, and share the code for free under the dual MIT and
    Apache 2.0 open-source framework.

  - If you "fork" (copy) the parser or transpilers to make your own version, you
    CANNOT claim you invented it, and you MUST change the name so it does not
    use "Krait Object Serialization Language", "KOSL", or the official project
    logo.

  - You CAN use the "KOSL" or "Krait Object Serialization Language" name and
    official logo to build, brand, and promote tools, utilities, or
    configurations created for the KOSL ecosystem, as long as it is clear that
    your tool is an independent community creation.

  - The word "krait" can be used completely freely by anyone for anything else
    outside of programming or serialization languages (like for games, snakes,
    clothes, or stories).